---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Research | Victor Solomon">
  <main class="light-page research-page">
    <section class="light-hero">
      <div class="light-kicker">Research</div>
      <h1>Machine learning methods for multimodal scientific data.</h1>
      <p>
        My research is centered on methods: multimodal fusion, representation learning,
        interpretable models, scientific foundation models, and dynamic systems.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="light-section research-statement">
      <div class="statement-aside">
        <span>Research thesis</span>
      </div>

      <div class="statement-body">
        <p>
          Scientific data is often heterogeneous, incomplete, high dimensional, and difficult
          to label. I am interested in learning systems that can align multiple data sources,
          reveal useful latent structure, and support scientific reasoning rather than only
          optimizing prediction accuracy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="light-section">
      <div class="light-section-head">
        <span>Focus Areas</span>
        <h2>Problems I am currently thinking about.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="research-columns">
        <article>
          <div class="research-icon">⌁</div>
          <h3>Multimodal fusion</h3>
          <p>
            How can models integrate heterogeneous views while preserving both shared
            structure and modality specific information?
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <div class="research-icon">◇</div>
          <h3>Interpretable representation learning</h3>
          <p>
            How can learned representations remain inspectable, stable, and meaningful
            for domain scientists?
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <div class="research-icon">◌</div>
          <h3>Scientific foundation models</h3>
          <p>
            How can foundation model ideas transfer to structured scientific data with
            limited labels and specialized modalities?
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <div class="research-icon">↝</div>
          <h3>Dynamic systems</h3>
          <p>
            How can models capture state changes, temporal dependencies, and evolving
            relationships in scientific signals?
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="light-section method-stack">
      <div>
        <span class="mini-label">Method stack</span>
        <h2>Tools and ideas I use.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="method-tags">
        <span>Multimodal learning</span>
        <span>Deep learning</span>
        <span>Latent variable models</span>
        <span>Foundation models</span>
        <span>Independent vector analysis</span>
        <span>Time series modeling</span>
        <span>Representation learning</span>
        <span>Scientific machine learning</span>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>